3:T48c,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you cure colour blindness?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There is currently no cure for inherited colour vision deficiency. Some tinted lenses and filters can enhance colour perception in certain situations, but they do not restore normal colour vision. Gene therapy research is ongoing but not yet available as a treatment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I get my child tested for colour blindness?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Colour vision testing should be part of your child's routine eye test. Early detection helps teachers and parents support the child's learning. It is especially important for boys, as 1 in 12 males has some degree of colour deficiency."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can colour blindness affect driving?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Colour vision deficiency does not disqualify you from driving a car in the UK. The DVLA does not require a colour vision test for standard (Group 1) driving licences. However, some professional driving roles may have colour vision requirements."}}]}0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"Colour Blind Test — How to Get Tested for Colour Vision Deficiency\",\"description\":\"How colour vision testing works in the UK, who should be tested, and how colour blindness might affect careers and daily life.\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/find/colour-blind-test\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"eyetest.co.uk\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"eyetest.co.uk\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"},\"dateModified\":\"2026-06-16\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\